{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRODUCT CARD — SLIDER VARIANT
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The commercial card that opens a product story row. Unlike "product-card-new", this variant carries only what is needed
to choose which bed to click: image, category, title, rating, price and one call to action. Specifications,
production claims and reassurances are told by the story cards that follow it in the row.

Beds whose colours are separate products merged with "my_fields.mcolors" — the same list the product page reads at
product-info.liquid — get a swatch row. Where the product page links away to the sibling's own page, the card keeps you
on the collection: every colour is rendered as a face inside this one card and the swatches switch between them. The
story cards after it are not touched, since they describe the bed rather than the fabric.

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* product: the product to render (required)
* eager: if set to true, the primary image loads eagerly. Only use on the first row of the page
* cta_text: the call to action label. Defaults to "Se sengen"
* class: additional classes added to the card root element
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign color_products = product.metafields.my_fields.mcolors.value

  comment
    The merged list is expected to hold every colour including this one, which is how the product page decides which
    swatch is current. If it does not — a colour left out of its own list — the card falls back to the single product
    rather than rendering a swatch row that cannot show the bed you are looking at.
  endcomment
  assign color_handles = ''
  for color_product in color_products
    assign color_handles = color_handles | append: ',' | append: color_product.handle | append: ','
  endfor

  assign self_key = ',' | append: product.handle | append: ','
  assign has_colors = false

  if color_products.size > 1 and color_handles contains self_key
    assign has_colors = true
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The sold-out modifier is set per face, since it belongs to the colour rather than to the card.
{%- endcomment -%}
<product-card class="story-card story-card--product snap-start group {{ class }}" handle="{{ product.handle | escape }}">
  {%- if has_colors -%}
    {%- for color_product in color_products -%}
      {%- assign is_active = false -%}
      {%- if color_product.handle == product.handle -%}
        {%- assign is_active = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- render 'product-card-slider-face',
        product: color_product,
        swatch_products: color_products,
        active: is_active,
        eager: eager,
        cta_text: cta_text
      -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- render 'product-card-slider-face', product: product, active: true, eager: eager, cta_text: cta_text -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</product-card>
